    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0392" n="320" xml:id="pg320"/>

                <head>No. 157.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3, 1882</date>.
                        (Received May 5.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous correspondence
                    upon the subject of the alleged forays of British Indians on American territory,
                    I have the honor to transmit to you herewith a copy of an approved minute of the
                    Privy Council of Canada embodying a report by the Right Honorable Sir J. A.
                    Macdonald, premier of the Dominion, to which is appended a report by
                    Lieutenant-Governor Dewdney, Indian Commissioner for the northwest territories,
                    on the subject.</p>
                <p>In transmitting this document I would beg to call your attention to the proposed
                    system of “permits,” which is submitted to the consideration of the United
                    States Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d212-a1.xml" xpointer="d212-a1"/>
